complete -c netop -n '__fish_seen_subcommand_from excel' -a inspect -d 'Report which rows match which Netrune switch and what is out of date, without writing. --free-ips also checks the unallocated addresses (pinging them), so the report shows which are free. Finds each sheets header row and columns, matches rows by serial, base MAC, IP, or hostname, and lists conflicts and unmatched rows. --sheet picks the sheets to read by name (any case) or by number, comma-separated for several; the heading numbers every sheet.'
complete -c netop -n '__fish_seen_subcommand_from excel' -a sync -d 'Write Netrunes current hostname, IP, manufacturer, model, serial, base MAC, and platform into the matched rows empty or out-of-date cells (status and last_seen with --fields). --refresh FIELDS rewrites those whole columns on every matched row, even cells that already agree in another notation and even under --fill-only, and stops them voting on which switch a row is. Each written cell is shaded by confidence in five steps: green certain (serial/MAC matched), blue strong (two keys agreed, or a new row), yellow fair (one IP or name filled a blank, or a sheet serial/MAC replaced), tan weak (one IP or name overwrote a value), red doubtful (--prefer broke a conflict); a switch not seen for 30 days drops one step; --no-shade turns it off and --comments adds a note with the old value. --remarks writes one brief note per row into the Remarks/Comments/Notes column (added when missing), worded as the techs own: what changed, Offline, Check: keys disagree, Duplicate of row N; the operators own text is kept. --free-ips (implies --remarks) marks addresses Free to use: never while a device Netrune knows (online or offline) or one seen in the last 30 days holds it; an empty row (no hostname, serial, or MAC) is free without pinging; a row naming something Netrune never saw is pinged and, if silent, asked about under --confirm in a terminal (y: Free to use (old entry), n: Allocated, offline) or settled with --accept-free/--reject-free IPS|all. The report suggests addresses for allocation, empty rows first. A remark saying reserved/DHCP/gateway is respected, and a Free to use is replaced once the address is in use. Formula cells, other columns, and other sheets are left alone. --confirm backs the original up, saves atomically, reads the file back to verify, and records an audit event; without it nothing is written.'
complete -c netop -n '__fish_seen_subcommand_from excel' -a export -d 'Write a new workbook: an Inventory table, a live Summary of formulas and a chart, and a Migration Tracker with dropdowns, lookups, and overdue highlighting. --confirm is needed only to replace an existing file, which is backed up first.'
complete -c netop -n '__fish_seen_subcommand_from excel' -a report -d 'Write a workbook of fixed-definition reports, one sheet each: active-aps, active-switches, transitions (renames, IP changes, IPs now on another device, serial/model changes, AP moves), switch-history and ap-history (every device online or offline, plus each replaced piece of hardware). Changes cover the last 30 days unless --since widens or narrows them. Each reports exact definition is written on the Report Info sheet. --confirm is needed only to replace an existing file, which is backed up first.'
